From e404fc1810ee6a301991487d4028bf9c833a2bb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: darkmaniac7 <darkmaniac7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:51:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Port cmpunlocker PR #55 SM reconfiguration override
 behind NVreg_CmpSmReconfig

CMP 170HX only (0x20C2 / 0x2082). New DWORD registry key CmpSmReconfig
(default 0, per device through NVreg_RegistryDwordsPerDevice). With 1, inside
the SEC2/Booter unlock window, after the PCIe retrain and before the ECC
recipe:

 1. RECONFIG_PLM 0x008200d8 <- 0xffffffff through the post-Booter payload,
    one Booter Load per attempt, up to two attempts, WPR2 blanked before each
    payload (as the ECC recipe does) and restored to the saved window after.
 2. Read OPT_GPC_DISABLE 0x00820350 and TPC STATUS 0x00820c38 + 4*gpc.
 3. gpc 0..7: BAR0 write 0x000000ff to the TPC RECONFIG OVERRIDE
    0x00820a40 + 4*gpc (a host write once the PLM is open, as upstream),
    read back the override and STATUS, log
    "CMP580: sm reconfig GPCn OVR(..)<-0xff read=.. taken|MISMATCH STATUS a->b".
    All writes are skipped if the PLM did not open; a GPC is skipped if its
    STATUS pre-read is invalid (0xffffffff / 0xbadxxxxx).
 4. "CMP580: sm reconfig done" line: PLM state, taken/mismatched/invalid,
    OPT_GPC_DISABLE, per-GPC STATUS before->after (fresh re-read), number of
    GPCs whose STATUS changed, and the implied TPC and SM count. Then the
    SS0/SS1/CFG1/LMR memory postcondition is re-checked, fatal if broken,
    exactly as after the retrain and the ECC recipe. Nothing else is fatal.

Rationale (PR #55): STATUS = DISABLE | DEFECTIVE | CTRL | (RECONFIG & ~OVERRIDE),
so the override can only release TPCs reserved through RECONFIG, never
defective or GPC-swept ones. Upstream measured on 0x20C2: OPT_GPC_DISABLE=0x85,
GPC4/GPC5 STATUS 0x01->0x00, +2 TPC = +4 SM, torch multi_processor_count
70->74. All four test cards logged two GPCs 0x01->0x00 under the 615
cmpunlocker build on 2026-10-17 (OPT_GPC_DISABLE 0x85, 0x0b, 0xa8, 0x23).

Placement: before the ECC recipe call rather than after it, so that no
Booter round runs after the ECC recipe's WPR/VPR/lock teardown; upstream's
order is the same (SM override, PCIe, ECC). With CmpEccRecipe=0 the two
placements are the same.

Difference from upstream: upstream opens RECONFIG_PLM in its always-on PLM
table next to OPT_PLM 0x8200fc, FEAT2 0x823b00 and PJTAG 0xc840/0xc848. This
tree's minimal table has none of those, so only RECONFIG_PLM is opened, and
only when requested. With the key absent or 0 nothing is written or logged.

Attribution and provenance: the register addresses, values, sequence and the
STATUS rationale come from cmpunlocker PR #55 "Add +4 more SMs" by Amogh
Munikote, landed as commit 6c442ee "Add more SMs" (2026-09-24) in
github.com/amoghmunikote/cmpunlocker. That project is GPL-2.0 and ships its
work as patches to NVIDIA's open-gpu-kernel-modules, where kernel_gsp.c is
MIT and the module is "Dual MIT/GPL". The code here is written fresh in this
tree's CMP580 style and is distributed under GPL-2.0 as a derived work.
